{% extends "synthesis_layout.jinja2" %}

{% block category_task %}
Write an authoritative historical-geographical encyclopedia article on the location: **{{ topic_name }}**.
{% endblock %}

{% block category_architecture %}
1. THE ORIENTING LEDE (NO SUBHEADING):
   - 1 concise paragraph defining the geographic location, ecological setting, historical jurisdiction, and regional significance.
2. SPATIAL & HISTORICAL BODY:
   - Organize into 2 to 4 '{{ body_heading_prefix }}' subheadings (e.g., `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Toponymy & Indigenous Landscape`, `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Settlement Patterns & Trade Networks`, `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Colonial Administration & Infrastructure`).
   {% if subtopics %}
   - Structure around: {{ subtopics | join(", ") }}.
   {% endif %}
3. FIELD RESEARCH & EXPLORATION:
   - Conclude with `{{ body_heading_prefix }} Research and Documentation` surveying early surveys, excavations, toponymic studies, and cartographic evidence in the records.
{% endblock %}